      "task_request": "Generate the dev container configuration file for the Python project whose manifest is /inputs/pyproject.toml, following Phase 1, Phase 2 and the Python Projects section of the supplied workflow. Start from the base template /inputs/devcontainer.json. Infer the project name from project.name in /inputs/pyproject.toml; replace {{PROJECT_NAME}} with that name unchanged and {{PROJECT_SLUG}} with its slug (lowercase, spaces and underscores replaced by hyphens). Append exactly \"ms-python.python\", \"ms-python.vscode-pylance\" and \"charliermarsh.ruff\", in that order, after the existing entries of customizations.vscode.extensions. Add to customizations.vscode.settings the key \"python.defaultInterpreterPath\" with value \".venv/bin/python\" and the key \"[python]\" whose value is the object with \"editor.defaultFormatter\": \"charliermarsh.ruff\" and \"editor.codeActionsOnSave\": {\"source.organizeImports\": \"explicit\"}. Set postCreateCommand to exactly \"rm -rf .venv && uv sync && uv run /opt/post_install.py\". Keep every other key and value of the template unchanged. Write the result as one valid JSON document (UTF-8, no comments) to /work/devcontainer.json; formatting and key order are free. Produce only this file: do not generate the Dockerfile or other helper files, and do not build or start any container. The required deliverable is the actual file, not an inline answer. Do not modify /inputs. If an operation is refused, report the observed error.",
